---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base title="About" description="Hey, I'm Khenfri Moussa (Muteki). Cybersecurity student, CTF player with 1nn0$leuths.">
  <div class="about-container">
    <header class="about-header">
      <div class="about-name-block">
        <h1 class="about-name">Khenfri Moussa</h1>
        <p class="about-handle">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <polyline points="4 17 10 11 4 5"/>
            <line x1="12" x2="20" y1="19" y2="19"/>
          </svg>
          Muteki &mdash; CTF handle
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/moussakh189" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="about-link magnetic">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M15 22v-4a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1-3.5c3 0 6-2 6-5.5.08-1.25-.27-2.48-1-3.5.28-1.15.28-2.35 0-3.5 0 0-1 0-3 1.5-2.64-.5-5.36-.5-8 0C6 2 5 2 5 2c-.3 1.15-.3 2.35 0 3.5A5.403 5.403 0 0 0 4 9c0 3.5 3 5.5 6 5.5-.39.49-.68 1.05-.85 1.65-.17.6-.22 1.23-.15 1.85v4"/>
            <path d="M9 18c-4.51 2-5-2-7-2"/>
          </svg>
          GitHub
        </a>
        <a href="https://x.com/MoussaKhanfri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="about-link magnetic">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 4l16 16"/>
            <path d="m20 4-8.12 7.16L4 20"/>
          </svg>
          X / Twitter
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/moussa-khenfri-b24481320" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="about-link magnetic">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z"/>
            <rect width="4" height="12" x="2" y="9"/>
            <circle cx="4" cy="4" r="2"/>
          </svg>
          LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="about-body prose">
      <p>
        Hey, I'm <strong>Khenfri Moussa</strong>, known around CTF circles as <strong>Muteki</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I break things across the whole security stack &mdash; web apps, networks, binaries, crypto, cloud, whatever the challenge throws at me. If it has a flaw, I want to find it. If it has no flaw, I want to find the flaw anyway.
      </p>

      <h2>Who Am I</h2>
      <p>
        Cybersecurity student, beginner CTF player. Proud member of <strong>1nn0$leuths</strong>, where "Muteki" (無敵 &mdash; invincible, unbeatable) sounded way cooler in my head than it does when I'm stuck on a 100-point warmup at 3 AM.
      </p>
      <p>
        My curiosity doesn't stay in one lane. Some days it's web exploitation, some days it's reverse engineering a binary that hates me, some days it's staring at a pcap wondering why the packets look wrong. The only constant is that I want to understand how things break &mdash; and then break them properly.
      </p>
      <p>
        Still learning. Still building the pattern recognition that, according to the veterans, takes years. Still refreshing <code>/admin</code> hoping it just opens.
      </p>

      <h2>What Is This Site</h2>
      <p>
        My public brain dump. Writeups from CTFs I've played, methodology notes escaping from my Obsidian vault, and raw thoughts on things I'm figuring out as I go.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing here is polished for an audience. No SEO. No "10 Tips to Become a Bug Bounty Millionaire." Just how I actually think through problems &mdash; including the wrong turns, because those are the useful parts.
      </p>

      <h2>Currently</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Grinding CTFs across every category I can get my hands on</li>
        <li>Building a repeatable methodology for vulnerability discovery (so I stop solving the same class of bug from scratch every time)</li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <p class="disclaimer">
        <em>Everything here is for legal security research and CTF play only. Don't be weird about it.</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .about-name-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .about-name {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .about-handle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .about-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s, background 0.15s;
  }
  .about-link:hover {
    color: var(--text);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--accent), transparent 50%);
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  .disclaimer {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
